sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Ingress Client
    participant Nginx as Nginx Reverse Proxy / Load Balancer
    participant BackendA as Backend A (Port 3001)
    participant BackendB as Backend B (Port 3002)

    Note over Nginx: Upstream Pool: round-robin (max_fails=3, fail_timeout=10s)

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over Nginx,BackendB: Phase 1: Healthy Alternating Round-Robin
        Client->>Nginx: Request 1 (GET /)
        Nginx->>BackendA: Forward to 3001
        BackendA-->>Nginx: 200 OK (X-Backend: A)
        Nginx-->>Client: 200 OK (X-Backend: A)

        Client->>Nginx: Request 2 (GET /)
        Nginx->>BackendB: Forward to 3002
        BackendB-->>Nginx: 200 OK (X-Backend: B)
        Nginx-->>Client: 200 OK (X-Backend: B)
    end

    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
        Note over BackendA: Failure Event: Backend A Terminated (SIGTERM / Port Crash)
        Client->>Nginx: Request 3 (GET /)
        Nginx->>BackendA: Forward to 3001 (Connection Refused / Timeout)
        Note over Nginx: proxy_next_upstream catches error / timeout
        Nginx->>BackendB: Transparent Immediate Retry to 3002
        BackendB-->>Nginx: 200 OK (X-Backend: B)
        Nginx-->>Client: 200 OK (X-Backend: B) (Client experiences zero 502 errors)

        Client->>Nginx: Request 4 (GET /)
        Note over Nginx: Backend A temporarily marked down (fail_timeout)
        Nginx->>BackendB: Forward to healthy Backend B
        BackendB-->>Nginx: 200 OK (X-Backend: B)
        Nginx-->>Client: 200 OK (X-Backend: B)
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over BackendA: Recovery Event: Backend A Restarted
        Note over Nginx: fail_timeout expires, probe succeeds
        Client->>Nginx: Request 5 (GET /)
        Nginx->>BackendA: Forward to restored Backend A
        BackendA-->>Nginx: 200 OK (X-Backend: A)
        Nginx-->>Client: 200 OK (X-Backend: A)
    end
